insert into documents (doc_type,title,source_url,doc_date,body) values ('news','Join the conversation: Zoning By-law open house set for July 22 | Township of Ramara','https://www.ramara.ca/news/posts/join-the-conversation-zoning-by-law-open-house-set-for-july-22/','2026-04-08','Join the conversation: Zoning By-law open house set for July 22 By Township of Ramara - Jul 14, 2026 Media Releases Ramara, Ont. / July 14, 2026 – The Township of Ramara is inviting residents, businesses, property owners and community organizations to attend an upcoming open house as part of the Township''s Comprehensive Zoning By-law Update. The introductory open house will take place on Wednesday, July 22, 2026, from 6 to 9 p.m. in the Council Chambers at the Township Administration Building (2297 Highway 12, Brechin). "Community input is an essential part of the Zoning By-law update process," said Mayor Basil Clarke. "The decisions made through this Zoning By-law update will help guide how Ramara grows while protecting the features that make our Township unique. Whether you''re a resident, business owner or property owner, we encourage everyone to attend the open house, ask questions and share their ideas." The open house provides an opportunity for the community to learn more about the project, meet with Township staff and the project team, ask questions, and share feedback that will help shape the future of land-use planning in Ramara. The Township''s Comprehensive Zoning By-law is being updated to align with the recently adopted Official Plan , current provincial planning legislation and the evolving needs of the community. Zoning establishes how land can be used throughout the Township and influences many aspects of everyday life, including housing, businesses, agriculture, waterfronts, transportation and community character. Residents who are unable to attend the open house can still participate by completing the online community survey and exploring the interactive mapping tool, both available until Aug. 5, 2026, at ramara.ca/ZoningUpdate . Hard copies of the survey are also available at the Township Administration Building, Ramara Centre and Ramara Public Library. Feedback received throughout the engagement process will help inform draft updates to the Township''s Comprehensive Zoning By-law. To complete the survey or to learn more about the Comprehensive Zoning By-law Update, visit ramara.ca/ZoningUpdate or email zoningupdate@ramara.ca. -30- Media Contact Melissa Gowanlock Manager of Communications & Community Experience 705-484-5374 ext. 322 mgowanlock@ramara.ca Subscribe Back to News Search Contact Us Corporation of the Township of Ramara 2297 Highway 12, PO Box 130, Brechin, ON, L0K 1B0 T. 705-484-5374 E. ramara@ramara.ca Sign up for our eNewsletter Stay up to date on the Township''s activities, events, programs and operations by subscribing to have notifications sent directly to your inbox. Sign Up Today!'),('news','Ramara Fire Danger Rating - High | Township of Ramara','https://www.ramara.ca/news/posts/ramara-fire-danger-rating-high/','2026-08-10','Ramara Fire Danger Rating - High - Jul 15, 2026 Public Meetings and Notices Update: The fire danger rating within the Township of Ramara has been updated to Moderate, effective 1:30 p.m. July 21, 2026. With the extreme heat and dry conditions, the fire danger rating within the Township of Ramara has been updated to HIGH, effective 9 a.m. today (July 15, 2026). A reminder that burning is not permitted when an air quality advisory is in effect. Residents are reminded to follow all requirements of the Township''s Open-Air Burning By-law and exercise caution when burning. Small campfires will still be permitted once air quality advisories are lifted, however, residents must exercise extreme care in supervision and the ability to extinguish the fire quickly, as conditions are favourable for rapid spread of fire through surrounding vegetation. Bona Fide Farmers are not permitted to burn oversized piles at this time. Residents are encouraged to use caution and monitor conditions closely, as fire danger ratings can change based on weather and environmental conditions. For more information on open-air burning requirements and current fire danger ratings, visit Open Air Burning | Township of Ramara . Subscribe Back to News Search Contact Us Corporation of the Township of Ramara 2297 Highway 12, PO Box 130, Brechin, ON, L0K 1B0 T. 705-484-5374 E. ramara@ramara.ca Sign up for our eNewsletter Stay up to date on the Township''s activities, events, programs and operations by subscribing to have notifications sent directly to your inbox. Sign Up Today!'),('news','July 2026 Ramara Bulletin | Township of Ramara','https://www.ramara.ca/news/posts/july-2026-ramara-bulletin/','2026-07-15','July 2026 Ramara Bulletin - Jul 24, 2026 Ramara Monthly Bulletin Important Dates and Opportunities Upcoming Council and Committee Meetings Monday, July 27: Special Meeting of Council re Interviews for Lagoon City Parks and Waterways Commission Vacancy Friday, August 7: Economic Development Committee Monday, August 10: Regular Council Meeting (including Committee of the Whole) Tuesday, August 11: Committee of Adjustment Tuesday, August 11: Property Standards Committee Thursday, August 13: Lagoon City Parks and Waterways Commission Friday, August 14: Joint Accessibility Advisory Committee Tuesday, August 25: Ramara Trails Committee Wednesday, August 26: Climate Action Committee Regular Council meetings may be streamed on the Township of Ramara''s YouTube channel and available in person in the Council Chambers in the Administration Building at 2297 Highway 12. Learn more about Council meetings, including reading Council Highlights, how to communicate with Council, and more at ramara.ca/CouncilMeetings. Civic Holiday Schedule The Township of Ramara administration building and facilities will be closed on Monday, August 3, 2026, for the Civic Holiday. Regular business hours will resume on Tuesday, August 4, 2026. Online services will remain available, including the following: Report an infrastructure or bylaw concern View interactive mapping for trails, zoning and by-law information Pay a bill Sign up for paperless billing And beyond See all online services at ramara.ca/OnlineServices . Municipal and School Board Election 2026 The 2026 Municipal and School Board Election will be held on Monday, October 26, 2026. Nominations are open from May 1 to August 21, 2026. Make sure you’re on the voters’ list , learn how to vote in the Township of Ramara, find out how to become a candidate or view the unofficial list of candidates . Learn more at ramara.ca/election . Nominations Thinking of running for Council? Nominations may be filed in person, or by an agent, with the Township Clerk during normal office hours prior to Nomination Day or on Nomination Day being Friday, August 21, 2026, between 9 a.m. and 2 p.m. If you wish to file a nomination, please make an appointment by emailing election@ramara.ca . If you are interested in running as a School Board Trustee, please note that nominations must be filed with the appropriate municipality, either the City of Orillia or the City of Barrie, depending on the position. Visit ramara.ca/election for more details. Voter Registration Elections Ontario is responsible for maintaining the Permanent Register of Electors for Ontario, commonly known as the Voters'' List. In order to vote in an upcoming Municipal or Provincial Election, you must be on the Voters'' List. Confirm, update, add, or remove your personal and/or property information through Elections Ontario''s Voter Registration Application until August 12, 2026. As of August 14, 2026, responsibility for the Voters'' List will transfer to local municipalities. Updates can be made directly with the Township of Ramara following this date. Further information about how to update, add, or remove personal and/or property information after August 14 will be available at ramara.ca/election or by contacting election@ramara.ca . Learn more about the 2026 Municipal and School Board Election Township News and Information Ramara welcomes Dr. Mehdi Dadashi T he Township of Ramara, in collaboration with the Couchiching Ontario Health Team (COHT) and the Orillia & Lake Country Physician Recruitment Committee (OLCPR), is pleased to announce that a second physician will be joining the Ramara Medical Centre in Brechin this fall. Dr. Dadashi will join Dr. Anoushka Mohammadiankhorasani (Dr. Mo), who has now opened her practice at the Ramara Medical Centre in Brechin, and is connecting with patients. Together, the two physicians will help expand access to primary care services for residents and strengthen local health-care options closer to home. Dr. Dadashi brings 20 years of clinical experience in family medicine and emergency care. Throughout his career, he has provided comprehensive primary care to patients of all ages, including chronic disease management, preventive care, health promotion, and urgent medical care. He has also worked extensively in hospital and emergency settings managing acute and complex medical conditions. In addition to joining the Ramara Medical Centre, Dr. Dadashi will provide services at Orillia Soldiers’ Memorial Hospital. How to Become a Patient: Priority will continue to be given to Ramara residents as part of this local physician recruitment initiative. Residents who have not yet registered and are interested in becoming a patient of Dr. Mo or Dr. Dadashi should register through Health Care Connect at: Phone: 1-800-445-1822 or call 811 Website: ontario.ca/HealthCareConnect Learn More and Register as a Patient Disaster Recovery Assistance for Ontarians (DRAO) Program Activated for April 2026 Flooding – Lake St. John Area, Ramara The Province of Ontario has announced that the Lake St. John area within the Township of Ramara has been designated as an activation area under the Disaster Recovery Assistance for Ontarians (DRAO) program for flooding that occurred in April 2026. Residents and property owners are encouraged to review the DRAO website , including the official activation area map , to determine whether their property is located within the designated activation area. Eligibility for the program is determined by the Province of Ontario. The deadline to apply for the program is November 16, 2026. Guidelines and application forms are available on the DRAO website . Learn More About the DRAO Program Lagoon City Canal Maintenance Update The Township of Ramara is pleased to advise residents that authorization from the Federal Department of Fisheries and Oceans (DFO) has been received to proceed with skimming and mechanical aquatic weed harvesting activities within Lagoon City''s canal system. Township crews have mobilized and canal weed harvesting operations began on July 21, 2026. We sincerely appreciate the patience and understanding of residents throughout this process and recognize the significant impacts the current condition of the canals has had on navigation, recreation and residents'' enjoyment of the waterways. Residents are encouraged to visit ramara.ca/canals for the latest harvesting routes and updates. Read the Full Lagoon City Canal Maintenance Update New Traffic Calming Policy Residents concerned about speeding and neighbourhood traffic now have a clear and consistent process for requesting traffic calming measures following Council''s adoption of the Township of Ramara''s new Traffic Calming Policy. Approved by Council at its meeting on July 13, 2026, the policy establishes a standardized approach for evaluating traffic concerns on eligible municipal roads. The new process, which is now in effect, ensures requests are reviewed fairly and consistently using technical data, community input and engineering best practices. Residents are encouraged to review the Traffic Calming Policy and learn more about the application process by visiting ramara.ca/TrafficCalming . Learn More About the Traffic Calming Policy Recreation Update Summer Camp Summer Camp is off to an amazing start at the Ramara Centre! The Recreation Team has been having a blast with campers, and this week marked an exciting milestone as we welcomed our very first off-site camp at the Joyland Beach Community Centre. The summer''s fun is far from over; there''s still a whole month of adventures, games, and memories to make! New Playground The Township is also thrilled to share that the brand-new playground at the Ramara Centre is officially open! It''s been wonderful seeing so many smiling faces enjoying the new play structure, and we can''t wait to see it become a gathering spot for families. Fall Flag Football Flag Football is back at the Ramara Centre this fall! Registration is underway and '),('news','Council Highlights - July 13, 2026 | Township of Ramara','https://www.ramara.ca/news/posts/council-highlights-july-13-2026/','2026-07-13','Council Highlights - July 13, 2026 - Jul 16, 2026 Council Highlights Announcements Mayor Clarke: Mayor Clarke encouraged residents to complete the County of Simcoe''s Organics Survey to provide feedback and help improve the County''s Green Cart program. The survey is available online at simcoe.ca/OrganicsSurvey and takes approximately 10 minutes to complete. Mayor Clarke announced that registration is now open for the Township''s Youth Flag Football program for ages 8 to 17. The program returns this fall following a successful spring season in partnership with SportsKlub. Residents can register at ramara.ca/recreation . Mayor Clarke reminded residents about the upcoming Zoning By-law Update Open House on July 22, 2026, from 6 to 9 p.m. at the Township Administration Building. Residents are also encouraged to complete the online survey and interactive mapping tool by August 5, 2026, at ramara.ca/ZoningUpdate . He encouraged residents to review the proposed zoning for their properties and surrounding areas and share their feedback. Mayor Clarke provided an update on the Township''s summer road maintenance program, noting that Township crews and contractors will be completing roadside mowing, gravel road improvements, dust control and line painting throughout the summer. Residents are reminded to use caution and slow down when travelling through active work areas. Mayor Clarke encouraged residents interested in running in the 2026 Municipal Election to attend the free Candidate Information Session on July 15, 2026, from 6 to 8 p.m. at Rotary Place in Orillia hosted in partnership with neighbouring municipalities and with the Ministry of Municipal Affairs and Housing. For more information regarding the 2026 Municipal Election visit ramara.ca/election . Mayor Clarke attended the Lake St. John Cottagers'' Association Annual General Meeting, where he met with residents to discuss local concerns, including flooding. He advised that staff will be reviewing the issues raised and providing follow-up where appropriate. Deputy Mayor Bell: Deputy Mayor Bell participated in several Canada Day celebrations throughout the Township, including the Bayshore Village Parade, Washago Canada Day Parade and visiting residents in Lagoon City. Deputy Mayor Bell attended the Grand Harbour Marina in Lagoon City for the Chamber of Commerce’s Classic Car Show and congratulated the organizers on another successful community event. Councillor Tuju: Councillor Tuju participated in the Washago Canada Day Parade alongside members of Severn Council and joined the community in celebrating Canada Day. Councillor Tuju attended the Township’s Volunteer Appreciation Dinner at the Brechin-Mara Legion and recognized the Township''s dedicated volunteers. She also congratulated Les Davy on being recognized for 50 years of volunteer service and thanked Sam Martino for providing a tour of the newly renovated, accessible lower level of the Legion. Councillor Bell: Councillor Bell attended the Township’s Volunteer Appreciation Dinner at the Brechin-Mara Legion and recognized the many volunteers who contribute to Township boards, committees and community organizations, including the Ramara Township Public Library Board, Lagoon City Parks and Waterways Commission, Rooted in Ramara, Ramara Historical Society and the Brechin Lions Club. Councillor Bell participated in the Lagoon City Canada Day Boat Parade and thanked residents for coming together to support one another following the storm that moved through the community on July 1, 2026. Councillor Bell congratulated Casino Rama Resort on celebrating 30 years of operation and recognized its continued contributions to local employment, tourism and community partnerships. Councillor Bell spoke to the success of the Ramara Chamber of Commerce Classic Car Show and congratulated everyone involved including volunteers and the Brechin Legion on another successful event. She also thanked the Couchiching Ontario Health Team for providing on-site Health Care Connect registration and reminded residents without a family physician that they can register by calling 811. Councillor Gough: Councillor Gough attended the Brechin-Mara Legion for the Township’s Volunteer Appreciation Dinner and thanked the Township''s volunteers and committee members for their ongoing dedication to the community. Councillor Gough participated in the Bayshore Village and Washago Canada Day parades alongside his grandchildren and enjoyed celebrating Canada Day with residents and visitors throughout the community. Committee of the Whole Presentations: Years of Service Recognition - Bill Kahler, Emergency Management Program Committee Mayor Clarke presented a Years of Service certificate to Bill Kahler and thanked him, on behalf of Council, for his tenure on the Emergency Management Program Committee. Deputations: Jen Dundas of Camp Couchiching regarding Support Consideration for a Safety Review of CLA2 Jen Dundas of Camp Couchiching gave a deputation regarding Support Consideration for a Safety Review of CLA2. The deputation was given in connection to Item 16.5.1. Council Motion from Councillor Snutch regarding a request for a review of operational safety for the Lake Country Airways water aerodrome location on Rama Road. View the Deputation Presentation from Camp Couchiching Open Public Forum: Lisa Sherin spoke to Agenda Item 16.5.1. regarding Councillor Snutch''s motion requesting a review of operational safety for the Lake Country Airways water aerodrome location on Rama Road. Laura Clementi spoke to Agenda Item 16.5.1. regarding Councillor Snutch''s motion requesting a review of operational safety for the Lake Country Airways water aerodrome location on Rama Road. Bob Brown spoke to Agenda Item 16.5.1. regarding Councillor Snutch''s motion requesting a review of operational safety for the Lake Country Airways water aerodrome location on Rama Road. Bruce Jackson spoke to Agenda Item 16.5.1. regarding Councillor Snutch''s motion requesting a review of operational safety for the Lake Country Airways water aerodrome location on Rama Road. Deborah Rosser spoke to Agenda Item 16.5.1. regarding Councillor Snutch''s motion requesting a review of operational safety for the Lake Country Airways water aerodrome location on Rama Road. Liane Spong spoke to Agenda Item 16.5.1. regarding Councillor Snutch''s motion requesting a review of operational safety for the Lake Country Airways water aerodrome location on Rama Road. Michael O''Brien spoke to Agenda Item 11.5.1. regarding the Water Financial Plan. Robert Lee spoke to Agenda Item 11.5.4. regarding the Florence Avenue Turnaround. Below are highlights of what Committee of the Whole recommended at its meeting held on Monday, July 13, 2026. These are subject to ratification by Council at its next meeting on August 10, 2026, unless pulled for ratification on the same day. Closed Session: Appointment of a New Commissioner to the Lagoon City Parks and Waterways Commission Committee of the Whole recommended receiving the report regarding the appointment of a new Commissioner to the Lagoon City Parks and Waterways Commission. Committee also recommended directing staff to arrange a Special Council meeting to interview applicants for the vacancy. The report was referred to the July 13, 2026, Council agenda for same-day ratification. Township of Ramara Industrial Park – Potential Purchase and Sale Committee of the Whole recommended receiving the report regarding the Township of Ramara Industrial Park and directing staff to proceed with exploratory next steps for potential buy-back options within the Industrial Park, pending Council''s future consideration and approval. The report was referred to the July 13, 2026, Council agenda for same-day ratification. Unopened Road Allowance – Balsam/Courtland/Patricia Drive Intersections Committee of the Whole recommended receiving the report regarding the unopened road allowance at the Balsam/Courtland/Patricia Drive intersections an'),('news','Ramara adopts new Traffic Calming Policy | Township of Ramara','https://www.ramara.ca/news/posts/ramara-adopts-new-traffic-calming-policy/','2026-08-10','Ramara adopts new Traffic Calming Policy By Township of Ramara - Jul 16, 2026 Media Releases Policy creates consistent process for reviewing neighbourhood traffic concerns Ramara, Ont. / July 16, 2026 – Residents concerned about speeding and neighbourhood traffic now have a clear and consistent process for requesting traffic calming measures following Council''s adoption of the Township of Ramara''s new Traffic Calming Policy. "Road safety is important to our residents and to Council," said Mayor Basil Clarke. "This new policy provides a transparent process for evaluating traffic concerns while ensuring decisions are based on objective criteria and the needs of the community." Approved by Council at its meeting on July 13, 2026, the policy establishes a standardized approach for evaluating traffic concerns on eligible municipal roads. The new process, which is now in effect, ensures requests are reviewed fairly and consistently using technical data, community input and engineering best practices. The policy applies to eligible local and collector roads within Ramara''s settlement areas and shoreline residential communities. Requests will be reviewed through a structured process that considers roadway characteristics, traffic conditions and neighbourhood feedback before projects are prioritized through the Township''s annual budget process. The policy takes a phased approach to traffic calming by considering measures that best match the identified traffic concern before moving to more significant infrastructure changes where warranted. This helps ensure solutions are effective, appropriate for the roadway and compatible with emergency services operations. "Having a consistent policy allows the Township to evaluate requests using the same criteria across the community," said Laura Pye, General Manager of Development and Infrastructure. "It provides a balanced approach that considers community concerns alongside technical data, road design, emergency access and available funding." Residents interested in requesting traffic calming measures should be aware that: · All requests will be reviewed using a consistent, evidence-based process. · Community feedback and technical traffic data will both be considered as part of the evaluation. · Not every request will result in traffic calming measures, as projects must meet the policy criteria and are subject to available funding. · Approved projects will be prioritized through future annual budget deliberations. Residents are encouraged to review the Traffic Calming Policy and learn more about the application process by visiting ramara.ca/TrafficCalming . -30- Media Contact Melissa Gowanlock Manager of Communications & Community Experience 705-484-5374 ext. 322 mgowanlock@ramara.ca Subscribe Back to News Search Contact Us Corporation of the Township of Ramara 2297 Highway 12, PO Box 130, Brechin, ON, L0K 1B0 T. 705-484-5374 E. ramara@ramara.ca Sign up for our eNewsletter Stay up to date on the Township''s activities, events, programs and operations by subscribing to have notifications sent directly to your inbox. Sign Up Today!'),('news','Notice of Special Council Meeting re Interviews for Lagoon City Parks and Waterways Commission Vacancy','https://www.ramara.ca/news/posts/notice-of-special-council-meeting-re-interviews-for-lagoon-city-parks-and-waterways-commission-vacancy-july-27-at-9-am/','2026-08-10','Notice of Special Council Meeting re Interviews for Lagoon City Parks and Waterways Commission Vacancy - July 27 at 9 a.m. By Township of Ramara - Jul 22, 2026 Public Meetings and Notices The Council of the Township of Ramara will hold a Special Meeting of Council on Monday, July 27, 2026, at 9 a.m. in the Council Chambers at the Township Administration Office. The purpose of this meeting is to interview the applicants for the vacant position on the Lagoon City Parks and Waterways Commission and select a Commissioner to fill the vacancy for the remainder of the 2026–2029 term. A portion of the meeting will be held in Closed Session. Members of the public who wish to attend the Council Chambers during the open session portions of the meeting are welcome. This meeting will be held in person only and will not be livestreamed. Dated this 22 nd day of July, 2026 Subscribe Back to News Search Contact Us Corporation of the Township of Ramara 2297 Highway 12, PO Box 130, Brechin, ON, L0K 1B0 T. 705-484-5374 E. ramara@ramara.ca Sign up for our eNewsletter Stay up to date on the Township''s activities, events, programs and operations by subscribing to have notifications sent directly to your inbox. Sign Up Today!') on conflict (source_url) do nothing;